# Design System Rules

## Token-first approach
- **Never hardcode colors, spacing, or typography values.** Use design tokens from `{{config.org}}/design-tokens`.
- Colors: use CSS variables (`var(--color-primary-9)`) or Tailwind token classes.
- Spacing: use the spacing scale (`var(--space-4)` or Tailwind `p-4`).
- Typography: use the type scale (`var(--text-sm)`) or Tailwind text utilities.
- Border radius: use token radii (`var(--radius-md)`) — never hardcode pixel values.

## Component architecture
- Every component in `packages/ui/` must export a `ComponentMeta` object alongside the component.
- ComponentMeta includes: name, description, variants, defaultVariant, slots, accessibilityRole.
- This metadata enables AI agents to use components correctly without reading implementation.
- One exported component per file. Internal helpers are fine if under 30 lines.

## Variant-driven design
- Use `class-variance-authority` (cva) for variant management.
- Variants are the API — props like `variant`, `size`, `color` map to visual states.
- Never use conditional class strings directly. Always go through cva.

## Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)
- Every interactive component must be keyboard navigable.
- Focus states must use `--color-border-focus` token.
- Color contrast ratio: 4.5:1 for text, 3:1 for large text and UI elements.
- Use semantic HTML elements: `<button>`, `<input>`, `<nav>`, not `<div onClick>`.
- All images need `alt` text. Decorative images use `alt=""`.
- Screen reader support: use `aria-label` for icon-only buttons.

{{#ifEquals config.design.motionLevel "full"}}
## Motion
- Import durations and easings from `{{config.org}}/design-tokens/motion`.
- Use `motion` library for animations. Never use raw CSS transitions for complex motion.
- Every animation must respect `prefers-reduced-motion` — wrap in motion's `useReducedMotion()`.
- Motion should explain state changes, not decorate. If removing the animation doesn't lose information, remove it.
- Duration guidelines: hover/press = instant (80ms), fade/slide = fast (200ms), page transitions = normal (300ms).
{{/ifEquals}}
{{#ifEquals config.design.motionLevel "subtle"}}
## Motion
- Use CSS transitions only. No JS animation library.
- Transitions limited to: opacity, transform, background-color, border-color.
- Duration: 150ms for hovers, 200ms for state changes. No longer animations.
- Always respect `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`.
{{/ifEquals}}
{{#ifEquals config.design.motionLevel "none"}}
## Motion
- No animations. No transitions. Instant state changes only.
- Do not import `motion` or add CSS transitions.
{{/ifEquals}}

## Dark mode
- Support both light and dark themes via `[data-theme="dark"]` selector.
- Use token aliases (`--color-bg`, `--color-fg`) that remap automatically.
- Never use hardcoded light/dark colors. The token system handles it.
- Test both modes for every component change.

## Figma integration
{{#if config.design.figmaFileKey}}
- Design source of truth is Figma file: `{{config.design.figmaFileKey}}`
- Use Code Connect to map Figma components to code components.
- Run `/figma-sync` after adding or modifying components.
- When implementing from Figma, use `/figma-implement <figma-url>`.
{{else}}
- Run `/figma-sync` to push the component library to Figma.
- When a Figma file is set up, add the file key to `.claude/settings.json`.
{{/if}}

## Forbidden patterns
- Hardcoded hex/rgb/hsl colors — use tokens.
- Inline `style=\{{}}` on React components — use Tailwind + tokens.
- `!important` in CSS — fix specificity instead.
- Custom breakpoints — use Tailwind's default responsive system.
- Importing from `packages/ui/src/` internals — use the barrel export.
